# SignalDesk — End User License Agreement

Version 1.1 · Effective 2026-10-02

This End User License Agreement (the "Agreement") is between Anhui Reallysec
Information Technology Ltd. (安徽斯普朗克信息技术有限公司, "Reallysec") and the
individual or entity that installs or uses the Software ("you"). By installing,
activating, or using the Software you agree to this Agreement. If you do not
agree, do not install or use the Software. If you accept this Agreement on
behalf of an organization, you represent that you have the authority to bind
that organization, and "you" refers to that organization.

**Please read the sections in bold with particular care. They limit Reallysec's
warranties and liability, restrict how you may use the Software, and set out
your responsibilities when you serve your own customers with it.**

## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"** means SignalDesk in the form delivered by Reallysec, including
  container images, deployment files, sealed (encrypted) feature modules,
  documentation, and any updates Reallysec provides.
- **"Documentation"** means the user and installation guides Reallysec publishes
  for the Software at https://reallysec.com/docs.
- **"License"** means the license key or license file issued by Reallysec that
  specifies your edition, feature set, node count, user count, and term.
- **"Edition"** means the Community or Enterprise edition, or a trial. The
  Enterprise edition and trials are stated in your License; the Community
  Edition is the Software used without a License.
- **"Enterprise Features"** means the features available only under a License,
  including those delivered as sealed modules.
- **"Subscription Term"** means the term of a paid License stated in your
  License or Order.
- **"User"** means an active account in the Software other than a customer
  portal account. Customer portal accounts, and deactivated or deleted accounts,
  are not counted as Users.
- **"Order"** means the quotation, purchase order, or other document under which
  you acquired the License.
- **"Your Data"** means the tickets, alerts, and other data that the Software
  processes on your behalf.
- **"Your Customers"** means the third parties to whom you provide managed
  services using a multi-tenant Edition.

## 2. License Grant

Subject to this Agreement and payment of the applicable fees, Reallysec grants
you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license, for the term
stated in your License, to install and use the Software for your internal
business operations, on no more nodes and for no more Users than your License
permits, and limited to the features of your Edition. Your employees and
contractors may use the Software on your behalf; you are responsible for their
compliance with this Agreement.

You may run the Software on your own hardware or on infrastructure that you
control and that a cloud or hosting provider operates on your behalf, provided
the provider does not use the Software for its own purposes.

Where your Edition includes multi-tenancy, "internal business operations"
includes delivering managed security or IT services to Your Customers,
including giving them customer portal accounts. **You are solely responsible for
the services you provide to Your Customers, for your agreements with them, and
for their use of the Software. You will indemnify Reallysec against claims
brought by Your Customers that arise from those services, except to the extent
the claim is caused by Reallysec's breach of this Agreement.**

A trial License grants the same rights for evaluation only, for the trial period
stated in the License.

Without a License, Reallysec grants you the same license free of charge and
without a fixed term, limited to the features of the Community Edition, five
(5) Users, and one node. Within these limits the Community Edition may be used
for commercial purposes, but only for your own internal business operations.
Reallysec may change the features of the Community Edition in later versions of
the Software.

## 3. Restrictions

**You must not, and must not permit any third party to:**

1. **bypass, disable, tamper with, or interfere with the License checks, the
   license key, or the mechanisms that keep Enterprise Features locked, or use
   any Enterprise Feature that your License does not cover;**
2. **decrypt, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer the sealed feature
   modules or any other part of the Software, except to the extent applicable
   law expressly permits despite this restriction;**
3. **offer the Software, or a substantial part of its functionality, to third
   parties as a hosted, managed, or software-as-a-service offering, except as
   Section 2 permits for multi-tenant Editions;**
4. **sell, rent, lease, lend, sublicense, distribute, or otherwise transfer the
   Software or the License, except as Reallysec agrees in writing;**
5. **share one License across more nodes, Users, hosts, or organizations than
   it permits;**
6. **delete, change, or hide any copyright, trademark, or licensing notice in
   the Software;**
7. **use the Software, or information obtained from its sealed modules,
   Documentation, or non-public behaviour, to build or help others build a
   product or service that competes with the Software;**
8. **use the Software in violation of applicable law, including export control
   and data protection laws.**

You may run benchmarks and performance tests of the Software. If you publish
the results, you must also publish the Software version, the configuration,
and the test method, so that others can reproduce them.

## 4. Ownership

The Software is licensed, not sold. Reallysec and its licensors retain all right,
title, and interest in and to the Software, including all intellectual property
rights. All rights not expressly granted in this Agreement are reserved.

If you provide suggestions or feedback about the Software, Reallysec may use them
without restriction or obligation to you.

## 5. Third-Party Components

The Software includes third-party and open-source components, listed in the
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file delivered with the Software. Each is licensed under its
own terms, which govern your use of that component. Nothing in this Agreement
limits your rights under those licenses.

## 6. Data

The Software runs in your environment. Your Data stays under your control, and
you are responsible for it, including under applicable data protection laws.

- **License service.** To activate and validate the License, the Software sends
  Reallysec's license service the license identifier, the product identifier
  and version, a hashed host fingerprint derived from machine identifiers, and
  activation status. It does not send Your Data. Without a License, the Software
  does not contact the license service. Offline activation, where your Edition
  includes it, sends nothing.
- **Update checks.** Unless you turn them off or use an offline License, the
  Software downloads a signed release file from the public GitHub Releases
  page of the Software once a day to check for updates. This sends no
  information to Reallysec.
- **Language models.** The Software sends prompts, which may include portions of
  Your Data, to the language-model endpoints you configure. Those endpoints are
  provided by you or your chosen provider under their own terms; Reallysec does
  not receive that data. **Output generated with language models may be
  incomplete or wrong, and the same input may produce different output. A
  qualified person must review AI-generated analysis, reports, and suggested
  actions before you act on them. You are responsible for your agreement with
  the model provider and for complying with the laws that apply to sending data
  to it, including personal information protection and cross-border data
  transfer rules.**
- **Support access.** If you give Reallysec access to your environment or to
  Your Data for support, Reallysec will use that access only to provide the
  support you requested, will treat Your Data as confidential under Section 12,
  and will not keep copies after the support is complete unless you agree.

## 7. License Checks, Updates, Support, and Preview Features

**A paid or trial License is checked when it is activated and, for online
activation, periodically afterward. If a check fails and is not resolved within
the grace period, or if the License expires or is revoked, the Enterprise
Features stop working and the Software continues as the Community Edition,
subject to its limits. Your Data is not deleted and you can still read and
export it. Records created with Enterprise Features remain in your database,
but those features cannot be used again until a valid License is applied.**

Reallysec may provide updates during the term of your License, and for the
Community Edition at its discretion. Support, service levels, and maintenance
are provided only as set out in your Order or a separate support agreement.

Features that the Software or the Documentation marks as preview, beta, or
experimental are provided for evaluation. Reallysec may change or remove them
at any time, and Section 9.1 does not apply to them.

## 8. Usage Verification

At Reallysec's written request, no more than once in any twelve (12) month
period, you will provide within thirty (30) days a written statement, signed by
an authorized representative, of the number of nodes on which the Software is
installed, the number of Users, and the Edition in use. Reallysec may also rely
on the activation records held by its license service. If the verification
shows use beyond your License, you will pay the applicable fees for the excess
use under Reallysec's then-current price list, and if the excess is more than
five percent (5%), you will also reimburse Reallysec's reasonable costs of the
verification.

## 9. Warranty

### 9.1 Limited warranty

For a paid License, Reallysec warrants that during the Subscription Term the
Software will perform substantially as described in the Documentation. If it
does not, and you notify Reallysec with enough detail to reproduce the problem,
Reallysec will use commercially reasonable efforts to correct the Software. If
Reallysec cannot do so within a reasonable time, either party may terminate the
affected License, and Reallysec will refund the prepaid fees for the remainder
of the Subscription Term. **This is your sole and exclusive remedy for breach
of this warranty.** The warranty does not apply to the Community Edition, trial
Licenses, preview features, or problems caused by modification, misuse, or an
environment the Documentation does not support.

### 9.2 Disclaimer

**Except for Section 9.1, and to the maximum extent permitted by law, the
Software is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for
a particular purpose, and non-infringement. Reallysec does not warrant that the
Software will be error-free or uninterrupted, or that it will detect, prevent,
or mitigate any security incident. Output generated with language models may
be inaccurate and must be reviewed before you rely on it. The Software supports,
and does not replace, your own security controls, monitoring, and professional
judgment.**

## 10. Intellectual Property Indemnity

10.1 If a third party claims that the Software, as delivered by Reallysec and
used in accordance with this Agreement, infringes that party's patent,
copyright, or trademark, or misappropriates its trade secret, Reallysec will
defend you against the claim and pay the damages and costs finally awarded
against you, or a settlement that Reallysec approves. This applies only to a
paid License, and only if you (a) notify Reallysec of the claim promptly in
writing, (b) give Reallysec sole control of the defence and any settlement, and
(c) provide reasonable cooperation at Reallysec's expense.

10.2 If the Software is, or Reallysec reasonably believes it may become, the
subject of such a claim, Reallysec may obtain the right for you to keep using
it, modify or replace it so that it no longer infringes while providing
substantially equivalent functionality, or, if neither is commercially
reasonable, terminate the affected License and refund the prepaid fees for the
remainder of the Subscription Term.

10.3 **Reallysec has no obligation under this Section for claims arising from:
third-party and open-source components (Section 5); output generated with
language models; modification of the Software by anyone other than Reallysec;
combination of the Software with products, data, or processes not provided by
Reallysec, where the claim would not exist without the combination; use of a
version other than the current one, where the current one would have avoided
the claim; or use in breach of this Agreement.**

10.4 **This Section states Reallysec's entire liability, and your exclusive
remedy, for third-party intellectual property claims. Reallysec's obligations
under this Section are subject to Section 11.**

## 11. Limitation of Liability

**To the maximum extent permitted by law, Reallysec is not liable for any
indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any
loss of profits, revenue, data, or business, even if advised of the possibility
of such damages.**

**Reallysec's total cumulative liability arising out of or relating to this
Agreement, under any theory of liability, will not exceed the fees you actually
paid to Reallysec for the Software in the twelve (12) months before the event
