## 12. Confidentiality

Each party will keep confidential the non-public information that the other
party discloses in connection with this Agreement and that is marked as
confidential or would reasonably be understood to be confidential. The
receiving party will use it only to perform this Agreement or exercise its
rights under it, and will protect it with at least reasonable care. Your Data
that Reallysec receives during support, your License, the sealed modules and
their keys, and non-public pricing are confidential information. This Section
does not apply to information that is or becomes public through no fault of the
receiving party, was already known to it, is independently developed by it, or
must be disclosed by law; in the last case, the receiving party will notify the
other party where the law permits.

## 13. Term and Termination

This Agreement takes effect when you first install or use the Software and
continues until it is terminated. When a paid or trial License expires, the
Software continues as the Community Edition under Sections 2 and 7. Reallysec
may terminate this Agreement if you breach Section 3 or fail to pay applicable
fees and do not cure the breach within thirty (30) days of notice.

On termination you must stop using the Software and destroy all copies, and
Reallysec may revoke your License. You may keep running the Software for up to
thirty (30) days after termination solely to export Your Data. Sections 2
(the indemnity for claims by Your Customers), 3, 4, 8, 9.2, 10.3, 10.4, 11, 12,
13, 15, and 16 survive termination.

## 14. Changes to this Agreement

Reallysec may update this Agreement. Each version of the Software is delivered
with the Agreement that applies to it, and the version number and effective
date appear at the top. For a paid License, the Agreement in effect when your
Subscription Term starts applies until that term ends, and an updated Agreement
applies from your next renewal. For the Community Edition and trials, an updated
Agreement applies when you install, or upgrade to, a version of the Software
that includes it.

## 15. Governing Law and Disputes

This Agreement is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China,
excluding its conflict-of-laws rules. The parties will first try to resolve any
dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement through good-faith
negotiation. If negotiation fails, either party may submit the dispute to the
Hefei Arbitration Commission for arbitration under its rules then in effect. The
seat of arbitration is Hefei, Anhui Province, and the language of arbitration
is Chinese. The award is final and binding on both parties.

## 16. General

- **Entire agreement.** This Agreement, together with your Order, is the entire
